A||||5||Greg Piet||How many wheels||||5
Z||000000||Greg Piet||10-07-1999||10:27 AM||||Ok, in a discussion with some friends about pos-a-traction, and limited slip diff's I thought of something.  How many wheels are actually powered in the fiero (1 or 2).  Sure one way to find out for me would to be to lay rubber, or to jack up the back end and see if I only one wheel spins with a little resistance on both, but i think this is easier!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||10-07-1999||02:37 PM||||As far as I can tell, my car has an "open" differential- non positrac. Even though on a wet road, it will spin both tires. I often wondered if there was a limited slip unit that would fit the fiero transaxle- but not many people really would need it. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phantom Rage||10-08-1999||12:00 AM||||Muuuhaaahaaaaahaaaaa!!! Check out this site. <A HREF="http://www.isuzuperformance.com/bills/drivdiff.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.isuzuperformance.com/bills/drivdiff.html</A> ||||reg||12
Z||000003||Shiner||10-08-1999||12:52 AM||||I don't mean to bust on your here, but, have you ever seen ANY kind of CAR that was powered by ONE WHEEL?!?  I would hope not.  It would be absolute murder in the snow for one thing.  The other guy was right, fiero's have an open differential.  You CAN get a quaiffe limited slip diff. for the fiero, at the cost of around $1500.  Pretty steep, especially considering that stock or mildy modded 2.8's don't need one..||||reg||12
Z||000004||Greg Piet||10-08-1999||01:02 AM||||Actually I feel much better.  I was surrounded 3 to 1 (me being the only one saying that both wheels were powered).  So...  I assumed I must have been on crack.  I was wondering why both wheels would be connected to the tranny if only one was powered, but i went by the democratic system and figured i must have been mistaken.||||reg||1
Z||000005||lowCG||10-08-1999||01:21 AM||||I remember seeing something that said all GM front wheel drive cars have a low percentage ltd slip,and since our cars use FWD transaxles,I figured we at least had that.<BR>Whether or not they still work after so many miles is another question.<BR>Stomped on it in a low speed turn the other day,and the back end skipped/chattered as it broke loose.This hasn't happened before,and I had just put in some Redline oil that has an additive for ltd slip differentials.||||reg||1
